how to create an IAM Policy

SageMaker permission to access an S3 bucket.

What you are doing here

You are on:

AWS → IAM → Policies → Create policy

Step 1: Specify permissions

You can see:

Select a service

Here, you must choose the AWS service for which you want to give permission.

For your lesson "How to push file from SageMaker to S3 bucket", select:

===

📦 Amazon S3

Then you will define what SageMaker is allowed to do with S3.

A typical permission is:

| Permission      | Purpose                       |
| --------------- | ----------------------------- |
| `s3:PutObject`  | Upload a file to an S3 bucket |
| `s3:GetObject`  | Read/download a file from S3  |
| `s3:ListBucket` | View files inside the bucket  |


====

Simple workflow

SageMaker Notebook / Studio
⬇️ requests permission through IAM Role / Policy
⬇️
Amazon S3 Bucket
⬇️
📁 Upload or access files

So, your next step in this screen is:

Click "Choose a service" → Search S3 → Select Amazon S3.

Then you can configure the required upload permissions and click Next.

====

Yes 👍 This is the JSON policy you need to allow access to your S3 bucket.

Policy explanation

====

{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "s3:PutObject",
        "s3:GetObject",
        "s3:ListBucket"
      ],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::insurance1hope",
        "arn:aws:s3:::insurance1hope/*"
      ]
    }
  ]
}

===

| Part                            | Meaning                                           |
| ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |
| `"Effect": "Allow"`             | Gives permission                                  |
| `s3:PutObject`                  | Allows uploading files to the S3 bucket           |
| `s3:GetObject`                  | Allows reading/downloading files                  |
| `s3:ListBucket`                 | Allows viewing the files in the bucket            |
| `arn:aws:s3:::insurance1hope`   | Refers to the S3 bucket itself                    |
| `arn:aws:s3:::insurance1hope/*` | Refers to **all files/objects inside** the bucket |


=====

Simple flow

Amazon SageMaker 🤖
⬇️ Uses IAM Role/Policy
⬇️ Gets permission
⬇️
S3 Bucket: insurance1hope 📦
⬇️
✅ Upload files
✅ Read files
✅ List files

Important

You must replace:

insurance1hope

with your own S3 bucket name if your bucket has a different name.

This policy gives SageMaker the required access to push/upload files from SageMaker to that specific S3 bucket.

